{"id": "ru-db8c01f74166.en", "jokeId": "ru-db8c01f74166", "locale": "en", "adaptation": "direct", "notes": "Line-by-line translation. The Russian subtext (traffic cops standing at crossroads collecting bribes) is weaker in English, but a cop who wants to stay at the intersection still reads as a traffic-cop habit. 'Мент' → 'the cop'. Same staging as ru.", "title": "The Crossroads", "location": "nebesa", "cast": ["sluzhivy", "ded"], "roles": {"sluzhivy": "traffic-cop", "ded": "god"}, "lines": [{"character": "narrator", "text": "A traffic cop died. He came before God.", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "narrator", "text": "God asks:", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "ded", "text": "Well, my son, did you do good to people?", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "sluzhivy", "text": "Yes, now and then.", "emotion": "smug", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "ded", "text": "And evil?", "emotion": "surprised", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "sluzhivy", "text": "That happened too.", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "ded", "text": "Well then, here are two roads, one to heaven, the other to hell.", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "ded", "text": "Whichever you choose, that's where you'll go.", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "narrator", "text": "The cop answers:", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "sluzhivy", "text": "Could I just stay here, at the crossroads?", "emotion": "smug", "pauseAfterSec": 0, "laugh": "big"}], "scenes": [{"location": "nebesa", "cast": ["sluzhivy", "ded"], "roles": {"sluzhivy": "traffic-cop", "ded": "god"}, "beats": [{"type": "move", "who": "ded", "to": "gate"}, {"type": "move", "who": "sluzhivy", "from": "off-left", "to": "left"}, {"type": "prop", "who": "sluzhivy", "item": "baton-striped", "action": "hold"}, {"type": "line", "ref": "l1"}, {"type": "line", "ref": "l2"}, {"type": "line"